{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans","id":7109,"title":"[EX3] Lunar Physicality - Tricksters & Shamans","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-09T17:10:42-08:00","id":7109,"title":"[EX3] Lunar Physicality - Tricksters & Shamans","content":"Among other biggies, we have two big facts from the devs about EX3 Lunars:<br /> 1) They're going to be very big on physicality, and<br /> 2) The archetypes embodied by their Castes are Warrior, Trickster, and Shaman (Castes presumably map to Full, Changing, and No Moons; no statement on the Attribute layouts).<br /> <br /> The former is important to highlight. This holds firmly enough that illusions are explicitly something Lunars don't do.* Given the second point, this came as a shock: illusions are a big tool in the toolbox for Tricksters and Shamans I tend to imagine. What Warriors will be up to doesn't puzzle me; physicality fits them like a glove, so they're not the focus of this thread.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">* I presume there may be effects that skirt this: I quite like the idea of a Lunar so persuasive his marks will actually see whatever he claims is there to see. It could be debateably more amusing if everyone so persuaded still sees what is actually there, but <i>believes everyone else sees something enough to doubt their own senses</i>, playing along and agreeing the emperor does indeed have clothes -- whether or not an emperor is even present.</span><br /> <br /> It also raises other questions. Is physicality meant to describe <i>all</i> Lunar Charms or is it just a prominent, prevailing trait? e.g. Can a Lunar just be that amazingly strong/smart/charming/whatever for an effect, or must there be some change worked for it? And how far can physicality be stretched, here: is it only about changing the Lunar herself, or can the Lunar work physical changes on the world and living things around her, such as with <a href=\"http://wiki.white-wolf.com/exalted/index.php?title=Knacks%3AInsidious_Lunar_Transformation\" target=\"_blank\">Insidious Lunar Transformation</a>? Does stuff like <a href=\"http://wiki.white-wolf.com/exalted/index.php?title=Ink_Monkeys,_vol._27%3A_We_Love_Lunars_(Part_II)#Wasp_of_the_Labyrinth_Trick\" target=\"_blank\">Wasp of the Labyrinth Trick</a> still have a home?<br /> <br /> The non-combat examples we've gotten have so far included fun with pheremones, glorious god-bodies, and brain modification. There's no telling yet if this means their Charms are all and only about changes, and then only to the Lunar. Though it does suggest such things are at least quite/most common in the set.<br /> <br /> I trust the devs know what they're doing and have no shortage of cool stuff for Tricksters and Shamans to get up to. I don't think they'd pick a paradigm that hangs those Castes out to dry for the third time in a row (barring broken mechanics). I just have a lot of blanks at the moment. Changing Moons and No Moons were kind of wanting for cool tricks before, and many of what few they <i>had</i> don't seem to fit anymore; I can't right now think of other cool stuff that might be taking its place.<br /> <br /> So, how about it, everybody? What do you think or want the bounds of Lunar physicality to be? And within that paradigm, what sort of awesome ideas do you have for Tricksters and Shamans to break out? Inquiring minds want to know!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">Inquiring minds will also not turn away further clarifications/examples from the team. &gt;_&gt;</span> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">... Please?</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T18:05:24-08:00","id":7119,"title":"","content":"Wasp of the Labyrinth Trick produces an ovipositor, so I'd bet on it staying. Lunars also conjure up phantom beasts of Essence and send them out to harry others or to sting and bite. Pacing about and ritual markings might also be favored elements.<br /> <br /> I do take issue with warriors intersecting exactly with physicality. War involves an awful lot of social activities and planning. Its execution hinges on communication. Physical Attributes just have you hitting people, taking hits, inflicting big pains and taking evasive action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T18:22:39-08:00","id":7125,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure I like this direction - I mean, it's better than no direction, but I'd rather have seen more emphasis on the Social and Mental shapeshifting we didn't see nearly enough of in 2nd Edition. I mean, things like growing additional brains so you can work on multiple projects at once or cooperate with yourself, or a charm emulating Luna that lets you shift motivation at will in exchange for effectively having inviolable intimacies (and being unable to gain more), or more shapeshifting that lets you impersonate people by having their Intimacies, Abilities, and general memories - hell, when you can eat their soul and usurp their Fate, small details like always greeting the door guard with a friendly insult or hating cashew nuts shouldn't be much of an issue!<br /> <br /> Trickster and Shaman... I'm hoping for Butterfly Eyes charms done right; the ability to run into an alley and hide behind a new wall or inside a conjured trashcan would be awesome, as would shenanigans like air bridges or invisible clothes. I'm also hoping that my Shaman will be able to cook together magic potions and set up wards using ingredients extruded from his own body or simply by carving symbols into the rock using his claws.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Aretii: &quot;As one of the players described it, 'After initiation, it was actually a relief seeing who had eyepatches or bandaged hands - you know what <i>they</i> sacrificed, instead of wondering what bits people cut out of their own souls to gain power.'&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/578-lord-sia","name":"Lord Sia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T18:48:04-08:00","id":7135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Sia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=7125#post7125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure I like this direction - I mean, it's better than no direction, but I'd rather have seen more emphasis on the Social and Mental shapeshifting we didn't see nearly enough of in 2nd Edition. I mean, things like <b>growing additional brains so you can work on multiple projects at once or cooperate with yourself</b>, or a charm emulating Luna that lets you shift motivation at will in exchange for effectively having inviolable intimacies (and being unable to gain more), or more shapeshifting that lets you impersonate people by having their Intimacies, Abilities, and general memories - hell, when you can eat their soul and usurp their Fate, small details like always greeting the door guard with a friendly insult or hating cashew nuts shouldn't be much of an issue!<br /> <br /> Trickster and Shaman... I'm hoping for Butterfly Eyes charms done right; the ability to run into an alley and hide behind a new wall or inside a conjured trashcan would be awesome, as would shenanigans like air bridges or invisible clothes. I'm also hoping that my Shaman will be able to cook together magic potions and set up wards using ingredients extruded from his own body or simply by carving symbols into the rock using his claws.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're thinking backward. Define a physical change, and then think of the benefits that it would produce. Don't think of the benefits first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T18:54:39-08:00","id":7136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans#post7109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) The archetypes embodied by their Castes are Warrior, Trickster, and Shaman (Castes presumably map to Full, Changing, and No Moons; no statement on the Attribute layouts).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I recall the context of this, and don't think it should exactly be read too much into.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This holds firmly enough that illusions are explicitly something Lunars don't do.* Given the second point, this came as a shock: illusions are a big tool in the toolbox for Tricksters and Shamans I tend to imagine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tricksters, maybe. Shamans? I don't quite see it as much.<br /> <br /> More importantly, while I can see resonance between Tricksters and illusions, I don't exactly recall stories that make it an especially intrinsic part of their repertoire.<br /> <br /> My mind reaches more towards Loki, who turned into a mare to lure away a necessary companion to an enemy of the Aesir or a fly to distract a dwarf at work on a wager, or to Br'er Rabbit tricking his enemies into tossing him into thorns that wouldn't harm him in order to escape, or Anansi binding up animals to fulfill a condition to receive stories, or snatching away their members to humiliate them.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't exactly know how that would manifest in Charisma or Manipulation Charms or what have you, but I'd consider it in the overall picture.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Although, if Lunars might impress you by drawing attention to their glorious God-Bodies, and the relevance of Attribute Charms is somewhat in being rather than doing, it might be that Lunar Charms for social Attributes operate according to a logic of assuming deeply ingrained body languages that shape intuitive responses to you.<br /> <br /> Like for All-Star Superman, where they go with the idea that part of how Clark Kent passes is that he's got such a fine level of muscle control that he can not only heavily modify his posture into a more meek and submissive stance, but he even looks more limp and flabby.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 11-09-2013, 10:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T19:16:13-08:00","id":7141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=7135#post7135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're thinking backward. Define a physical change, and then think of the benefits that it would produce. Don't think of the benefits first.</div> </div> </div> </div>Growing additional brains is a particular one I dislike, just because it seems far too Tyranid.<br /> <br /> When I think about it, I realise I have two basic standards of inspiration for Lunars; shapeshifting and totem/anthropomorphism mythology. When it comes to implementation in the context of Exalted, for the former, that generally means changing from one thing into another, either in whole or in part, or kind of stretching out or rearranging what you already have. For the latter, sometimes, occasionally, it means adopting some resonant animal traits or mechanisms, but mostly it means adopting the logic of <i>why</i> totem mythology is used, and reapplying it to people. Like, Renard is a fox not because he does anything that necessitates the biology of a fox, but because the idea of fox conveys his persona. So just think of what signifiers in human forms convey personas, at least in our collective narratives, and imagine the same basic appearance shifting through those signifiers. Like the difference between Superman and Clark Kent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T19:31:40-08:00","id":7149,"title":"","content":"One idea for a physical shaman is going the &quot;willing possession&quot; route - perhaps Charms that give a possessing spirit benefits, or grant a better synergy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T21:56:09-08:00","id":7184,"title":"","content":"People tend to forget that illusions are fake, or false, and physicality is what's real. With Lunars being very physical, they don't need illusions, they become and empower the effects, they make the &quot;illusionary&quot; effects real.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T22:23:32-08:00","id":7193,"title":"","content":"So when they disappear into an alleyway, do they turn into trashcans, turn into mice, turn into stones, merge with the walls, or do they simply glower at whoever is looking at them with such animosity and provocation of fear that the guards chasing him know better than to look for him there?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T22:38:40-08:00","id":7195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brasstreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=7193#post7193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So when they disappear into an alleyway, do they turn into trashcans, turn into mice, turn into stones, merge with the walls, or do they simply glower at whoever is looking at them with such animosity and provocation of fear that the guards chasing him know better than to look for him there?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FFF0F5\">Pay no attention to this tex</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/370-oriares","name":"Oriares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T00:42:17-08:00","id":7217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=7141#post7141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Growing additional brains is a particular one I dislike, just because it seems far too Tyranid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Lunars are not the Brood Queen or Alex Mercer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T01:37:05-08:00","id":7237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brasstreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=7193#post7193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So when they disappear into an alleyway, do they turn into trashcans, turn into mice, turn into stones, merge with the walls, or do they simply glower at whoever is looking at them with such animosity and provocation of fear that the guards chasing him know better than to look for him there?</div> </div> </div> </div>If this is the way the &quot;no illusions&quot; thingy is going to work, I could be down with this shit. Because with the first snippets of info I, too, was afraid of the Trickster/Shaman concept not working too well. I am more optimistic now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T05:02:08-08:00","id":7292,"title":"","content":"I wonder if trying to shoehorn Lunars into some kind of archetypes is a worthwile endeavour.<br /> <br /> I mean, we don't play archetypes, we're playing characters. Creating a rigid frame of three possible archetypes only lowers the amount of ideas for a character you can come up with.<br /> <br /> Solars don't have rigid archetypes, Abyssals don't have rigid archetypes, even Dragon-Blooded don't really have rigid archetypes they must adhere to.<br /> <br /> I don't know if it wouldn't be more apropriate to just create a Lunar charmset with a coherent theme in mind, in this case phsyciality and transformation I guess, and just let people play around with it.<br /> <br /> Saying that every Lunar has to be a wrrior, a trickster, or a shaman, is not productive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/620-arrakiz","name":"Arrakiz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar620_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T06:23:15-08:00","id":7302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arrakiz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=7292#post7292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if trying to shoehorn Lunars into some kind of archetypes is a worthwile endeavour.<br /> <br /> I mean, we don't play archetypes, we're playing characters. Creating a rigid frame of three possible archetypes only lowers the amount of ideas for a character you can come up with.<br /> <br /> Solars don't have rigid archetypes, Abyssals don't have rigid archetypes, even Dragon-Blooded don't really have rigid archetypes they must adhere to.<br /> <br /> I don't know if it wouldn't be more apropriate to just create a Lunar charmset with a coherent theme in mind, in this case phsyciality and transformation I guess, and just let people play around with it.<br /> <br /> Saying that every Lunar has to be a wrrior, a trickster, or a shaman, is not productive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Solars don't have 'rigid' archetypes, but they have broad archetypes. They're useful tools to guiding how we think about the splats, and helping us map inspirations from other media onto the framework that Exalted provides. I can certainly build a night caste in ways that don't utilize any night caste skills, and build her with straight combat stats and sorcery, but it's easier to build at least some sneaky-type-traits in there, which also makes it easy to brainstorm characters by looking at other sneaky-type characters.<br /> <br /> I don't think we're saying that every Lunar has to be a cookie-cutter warrior, trickster or shaman. But having some concepts as starting points is a useful thing... and I'd go so far as to say a neccessary thing, given how much trouble Lunars have historically had with displaying their core themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/894-skeptic-tank","name":"Skeptic Tank","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar894_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T07:52:38-08:00","id":7341,"title":"","content":"Hell, &quot;trickster&quot; is far broader an archetype than &quot;diplomat,&quot; and &quot;shaman&quot; is just as broad as &quot;priest.&quot; With such flexible terms, I find I really don't mind being &quot;locked&quot; into something as broad and encompassing as <i>any</i> of those three.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T09:05:48-08:00","id":7381,"title":"","content":"If I want to make a pro-social character, something of a leader, let's say, than I don't care one way or another for &quot;trickster&quot; or a &quot;shaman&quot; or a &quot;warrior&quot;. If I want to make a quirky anti-social genius character, than I don't care one way or another for &quot;trickster&quot; or a &quot;shaman&quot; or a &quot;warrior&quot;. If I want to make a mercenary goon with only motvation being gold, I don't care one way or another for &quot;trickster&quot; or a &quot;shaman&quot; or a &quot;warrior&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't think it's necessary to think in those categories. It's like saying &quot;we're gonna give players the ability to pick powers and abilities whcih fit with their characters being a trickster or a shaman or a warrior and nothing more&quot;. And I don't see a point in doing that.<br /> <br /> Just pick a theme and make mechanics that will compliment the theme. If it's physical prowess, thank great, that's ok. I'm sure people can come up with archetypes that will work best with this theme on their own, the devs shouldn't limit themselves to creating mechanics that will describe only these three archetypes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/620-arrakiz","user":"Arrakiz","date":". 11-10-2013, 12:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/620-arrakiz","name":"Arrakiz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar620_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T09:23:42-08:00","id":7394,"title":"","content":"How is this set of archetypes such a problem for concepts compared to &quot;general, priest, scholar, rogue, diplomat&quot; or more abstract shit that other Exalts get? Is it because there are less of them? Is it these specific archetypes? You seem to still not have addressed why this is an issue for Lunars that it isn't for Solars and Abyssals.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T09:32:34-08:00","id":7402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=7394#post7394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is this set of archetypes such a problem for concepts compared to &quot;general, priest, scholar, rogue, diplomat&quot; or more abstract shit that other Exalts get? Is it because there are less of them? Is it these specific archetypes? You seem to still not have addressed why this is an issue for Lunars that it isn't for Solars and Abyssals.<br /> <br /> And stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I do have a problem with thinking in terms of five Solar Caste archetypes. You know that saying that every Twilight is a srocerer is not a good thing.<br /> <br /> But the thing is- Solar charms aren't created by thinking &quot;let's make something that will work with the concepts of a fighter, priest, scholar, rogue aand diplomat&quot;. They're created by looking at the 25 abilities that describe every action you can possibly take in the game and extrapolate it on superhuman level. And only afterwards they are put into group of fives, based on those archetypes. But you are free to ignore those archetypes, sure you have the anima power and yeah that's a thing. But you don't have to build your character as a diplomat, if you are an Eclpse, or as a fighter, if you are a Dawn.<br /> <br /> That's why I think the line of thought spanning from &quot;Lunars are tricksters, warriors and shamans&quot; goes nowhere. It's much more productive to go back to the natural roots of the Lunar power- atributes. Archetypes will form on their own afterwards and should at no point be something that influences the process of creating Lunar powers.<br /> <br /> Anima powers, sure, I can see that. But not actual charms, come on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/620-arrakiz","user":"Arrakiz","date":". 11-10-2013, 12:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/620-arrakiz","name":"Arrakiz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar620_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T10:50:45-08:00","id":7490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arrakiz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=7402#post7402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I do have a problem with thinking in terms of five Solar Caste archetypes. You know that saying that every Twilight is a sorcerer is not a good thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Blaque clearly listed the caste archetype as scholar, not sorcerer, so what the hell are you arguing about?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But the thing is- Solar charms aren't created by thinking &quot;let's make something that will work with the concepts of a fighter, priest, scholar, rogue aand diplomat&quot;. They're created by looking at the 25 abilities that describe every action you can possibly take in the game and extrapolate it on superhuman level. And only afterwards they are put into group of fives, based on those archetypes. But you are free to ignore those archetypes, sure you have the anima power and yeah that's a thing. But you don't have to build your character as a diplomat, if you are an Eclpse, or as a fighter, if you are a Dawn.<br /> <br /> That's why I think the line of thought spanning from &quot;Lunars are tricksters, warriors and shamans&quot; goes nowhere. It's much more productive to go back to the natural roots of the Lunar power- atributes. Archetypes will form on their own afterwards and should at no point be something that influences the process of creating Lunar powers.<br /> <br /> Anima powers, sure, I can see that. But not actual charms, come on. </div> </div> </div>Those archetypes are really easy to have material slot into. They're professional descriptions of roles in society that we get shaped for all the time. Lunars a trickier, because few people are so fully outside of the society that they were born into. The kind of people that societies tell cautionary tales about.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T11:12:56-08:00","id":7512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=7490#post7490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those archetypes are really easy to have material slot into. They're professional descriptions of roles in society that we get shaped for all the time. Lunars a trickier, because few people are so fully outside of the society that they were born into. The kind of people that societies tell cautionary tales about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uuuuuum... Fuck that? Sorry, but why would the choice of the type of Exalt determine the role I play in the society? Shouldn't I decide that for my character, in acordance with the GM? Is it really ok to put a statement like &quot;the social role of any Lunar can only be a trickster, a warrior or a shaman and nothing else&quot;? Is that really smart?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/620-arrakiz","name":"Arrakiz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar620_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T12:22:37-08:00","id":7561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arrakiz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=7512#post7512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uuuuuum... Fuck that? Sorry, but why would the choice of the type of Exalt determine the role I play in the society? Shouldn't I decide that for my character, in acordance with the GM? Is it really ok to put a statement like &quot;the social role of any Lunar can only be a trickster, a warrior or a shaman and nothing else&quot;? Is that really smart?</div> </div> </div> </div>If the Lunar theme is linked to outsiders, then it makes sense for the usual way to look at them to come from the perspective of &quot;what sort of person is an outsider.&quot; It's not a straight dichotomy, obviously - it depends on how the themes are portrayed how exactly this works - but while you can step away from Lunar themes to an extent, there will come a point when anyone lookign at it will go &quot;well yes OK, but why is this person a Lunar?&quot;<br /> <br /> EDIT: It's not that the social role of the character will be that, but look at the Solars. Their social powers tend to reinforce the idea that they lead, though they can do other things; I'd expect Lunars to take a different tack, maybe guiding and supporting, sometimes by terrifying people away from what they don't want to do, but not leading quite so much. You could still make a Lunar leader but the powers would lend themselves slightly better to outsider cunning than straightforward leading.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","user":"MorkaisChosen","date":". 11-10-2013, 03:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T12:29:43-08:00","id":7566,"title":"","content":"I wonder what quotes did to this forum to make it hate them so. :/ If I take too long, I also don't love how it apparently loses the server connection, and feels the need to remind me every minute or so... Am I alone in having this issue?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=7119#post7119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasp of the Labyrinth Trick produces an ovipositor, so I'd bet on it staying. Lunars also conjure up phantom beasts of Essence and send them out to harry others or to sting and bite. Pacing about and ritual markings might also be favored elements.</div> </div> </div> </div> True on the ovipositor and ritual markings. For the latter, I'm hopeful that territory Charms will return, and actually be worthwhile this time. Phantom beasts I'm not so sure about; I'd love to see them, but they didn't seem to fit with how much the Lunar's physicality was stressed. Releasing flesh and blood creatures from their body seemed like it might sub in handily, though. And I may have also been reading too much into physicality.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I do take issue with warriors intersecting exactly with physicality. War involves an awful lot of social activities and planning. Its execution hinges on communication. Physical Attributes just have you hitting people, taking hits, inflicting big pains and taking evasive action. </div> </div> </div>Then I shall clarify my meaning. My point was not that physicality provides everything a warrior needs. Just that examples of things warriors could get out of physicality in the field of... warrior-ing come more easily to mind. My mind, anyway.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=7136#post7136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I recall the context of this, and don't think it should exactly be read too much into.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you clarify please?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tricksters, maybe. Shamans? I don't quite see it as much. </div> </div> </div>Granted. I suppose I was mentally extending 'illusions' to cover 'anything not physically real,' which might rule out quite a bit of other things, such as some sort of shamanistic vision quest for insight. Pretty sure I was going a bit far if I did so; facilitating it in the Lunar or others with a drug the Lunar's body produces or something might be able to do it. On which note, even if illusions are out, releasing/injecting hallucinatory toxins seems feasible.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My mind reaches more towards Loki, who turned into a mare to lure away a necessary companion to an enemy of the Aesir or a fly to distract a dwarf at work on a wager, or to Br'er Rabbit tricking his enemies into tossing him into thorns that wouldn't harm him in order to escape, or Anansi binding up animals to fulfill a condition to receive stories, or snatching away their members to humiliate them.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't exactly know how that would manifest in Charisma or Manipulation Charms or what have you, but I'd consider it in the overall picture. </div> </div> </div>Yes, those are definitely great trickster influences I'd hope we see. Translating them into physicality has been the stumbling block for me. Though you may be on the right track in your edit; I've tended to think in terms of gross physical changes for Lunar effects, instead of more subtle notions of body language. This may be a part of the issue I'm having with examples.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=7141#post7141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I think about it, I realise I have two basic standards of inspiration for Lunars; shapeshifting and totem/anthropomorphism mythology. When it comes to implementation in the context of Exalted, for the former, that generally means changing from one thing into another, either in whole or in part, or kind of stretching out or rearranging what you already have. For the latter, sometimes, occasionally, it means adopting some resonant animal traits or mechanisms, but mostly it means adopting the logic of <i>why</i> totem mythology is used, and reapplying it to people. Like, Renard is a fox not because he does anything that necessitates the biology of a fox, but because the idea of fox conveys his persona. So just think of what signifiers in human forms convey personas, at least in our collective narratives, and imagine the same basic appearance shifting through those signifiers. Like the difference between Superman and Clark Kent.</div> </div> </div> </div>This intrigues me and sounds like fertile ground. The plans they've mentioned for the Spirit Shape definitely seem to work with the totem animal idea, but that needn't be the only such avenue. For applying the logic to human interactions, I'm interested, but may be a bit fuzzy on the actual execution there. How do you think it might work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T15:22:07-08:00","id":7690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arrakiz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=7512#post7512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uuuuuum... Fuck that? Sorry, but why would the choice of the type of Exalt determine the role I play in the society? Shouldn't I decide that for my character, in acordance with the GM? Is it really ok to put a statement like &quot;the social role of any Lunar can only be a trickster, a warrior or a shaman and nothing else&quot;? Is that really smart?</div> </div> </div> </div>You do that if you play a Solar or Exigent. If you're playing anything else, some material will come prepackaged, without the option to remove it. This is known as &quot;flavor&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T17:54:17-08:00","id":7770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=7217#post7217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed. Lunars are not the Brood Queen or Alex Mercer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah.<br /> <br /> ...Patching multiple brains together is totally a Liminal thing! (Have I mentioned yet on this forum that I see Alex Mercer as a Liminal of the Flesh Aspect? Well, now I have.)<br /> <br /> But getting back on topic, I'm glad that the Lunars aren't being taken down that route.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T17:56:47-08:00","id":7772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=7770#post7770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah.<br /> <br /> ...Patching multiple brains together is totally a Liminal thing! (Have I mentioned yet on this forum that I see Alex Mercer as a Liminal of the Flesh Aspect? Well, now I have.)<br /> <br /> But getting back on topic, I'm glad that the Lunars aren't being taken down that route.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, putting someone else's severed head on you to gain their memories is Liminal. Patching multiple brains together is just the internet/Alchemical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/781-chained-divinity","name":"Chained Divinity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar781_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T18:12:46-08:00","id":7780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=7690#post7690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You do that if you play a Solar or Exigent. If you're playing anything else, some material will come prepackaged, without the option to remove it. This is known as &quot;flavor&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, this is known as &quot;constrain&quot;. Granted, Neph did a <i>wonderous</i> job of convincing everybody that these are one and the same thing, but actaully they aren't. flavor is, by definition, something optional and something you can change and mess around with.<br /> <br /> There is literally no point in putting this artifical constrain there, outside of just putting it there for it's own sake.<br /> <br /> And it's not even right that only Solars have a free pass, pretty much everyone has a free pass, except Alchemicals. Abyssals don't have pre-determined archetypes, they can choose their social role freely. Sure, it's harder for them to be super social among the living, because they are so often very creepy, but it's just a matter of finding the right crowd. Dragon Blooded? Princes of the Earth, they can do whatever they want. Infernals can just get the hell out of, well, Hell and roam Creation free. Even the Sidereal can go ronin and completely ignore their supposed &quot;duty&quot; So long as long they aren't actively trying to harm the duties of their brethren, they're gonna be fine.<br /> <br /> What's so special about Lunars that makes it so they can only ever be a trickster, a warrior, or a shaman, in any given group? Why can't they be the leader? Or the scholar? Or the charming belly dancer? Or a pizza delivery guy? Or a poet, or a messanger, or a knight in shiny armour?<br /> <br /> I'm not playing a Lunar becasue I want to play a trickster/warrior/shaman, I'm playing a Lunar because I want to play a shape-changing, barbarian, beast-hero who can bench-press a Yedim and devour hearts of the mightiest beasts for theis strenght and who can turn into a horse, seduce a woman and create weird and yet suspicioudly strong offspring! I don't give a damn about the &quot;role in the society&quot; you want to shoehorn me into and not because I'm just being a naive rebel, but because I don't find it fun when I am told which role I must play, by anybody else than my GM and myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/620-arrakiz","user":"Arrakiz","date":". 11-10-2013, 09:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/620-arrakiz","name":"Arrakiz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar620_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T18:24:04-08:00","id":7791,"title":"","content":"People seem to be confusing possessing attributes and skillsets of archetypes as being that archetype. The three archetypes of Warrior, Trickster, and Shaman, are given to easily define the kinds of skillsets or attributes the player would get by choosing that package for their character. This has been the case for castes since 1st edition.This is not saying you must play your character in &quot;this way&quot; it's saying, here's the default package of tools you get for choosing this for your character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T00:51:01-08:00","id":7921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arrakiz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=7780#post7780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What's so special about Lunars that makes it so they can only ever be a trickster, a warrior, or a LPshaman, in any given group? Why can't they be the leader? Or the scholar? Or the charming belly dancer? Or a pizza delivery guy? Or a poet, or a messanger, or a knight in shiny armour?</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Leader? Leads through might nd example as a warrior. Through devious cleverness he's a trickster. Through wisdom and advice he's a shaman type.<br /> <br /> Scholar? Shaman, if he's the wise kind. Warrior or trickster for snooping around. All could be sorcerers depending on how they use their magic.<br /> <br /> Belly dancer? She's a trickster. The pizza delivery guy? Trickster, whether he fucks the lonely housewife after delivering some extra sausage or gets frozen for 1000 years.<br /> <br /> I think you misunderstand what those three categories are. They're not strict concepts forced on you.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T03:18:11-08:00","id":7953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=7791#post7791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People seem to be confusing possessing attributes and skillsets of archetypes as being that archetype. The three archetypes of Warrior, Trickster, and Shaman, are given to easily define the kinds of skillsets or attributes the player would get by choosing that package for their character. This has been the case for castes since 1st edition.This is not saying you must play your character in &quot;this way&quot; it's saying, here's the default package of tools you get for choosing this for your character.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point exactly. I just think that trying to base Lunar abilities/powers/mechanics off of the archetypes of shaman/warrior/trickster is an exercise in futility, because not every Lunar is a shaman, a warrior, or a trickster and trying to come up with powers and abilities that will only ever compliment and describe those three archetypes is not broad enough way to look at the Lunar power set.<br /> <br /> What we should be doing, is looking at the basic root of Lunar theme- monstrous, barbaric, shapchanging godly being, and try to extrapolate what abilities does somebody like this have, without asking a single question about her personality, culture, or a social role.<br /> <br /> And if than turns out that Lunars aren't adequetely equiped to play the Trickster, or a Shaman, or a Warrior, or a Leader, or a Belly Dancer, or a Pizza Delivery Guys part? That means they have a little harder job trying to fit in those archetypes and you should try coming up with custom charms and abilties to makes it work better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/620-arrakiz","name":"Arrakiz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar620_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T03:57:11-08:00","id":7963,"title":"","content":"...you're seeing chains where none exist, Arrakiz.<br /> <br /> When they say &quot;trickster, warrior, shaman,&quot; they're not saying &quot;this is the only thing you can do with a Lunar.&quot; They're saying &quot;we're looking at trickster/warrior/shaman characters from media that inspired Exalted for inspiration in terms of what Lunars should be able to do.&quot;<br /> <br /> So, y'know, monstrous characters, barbaric characters, shapechanging godly beings. Like you said.<br /> <br /> Trickster/warrior/shaman isn't about &quot;social role&quot; or personality, or culture. It's about a series of genre conventions. As always, we will be encouraged to explore these genre conventions with our characters and play out or subvert them at our whim: I'd be very much surprised if Belly Dancing courtesan Lunar wasn't possible, or if Pizza Delivery Guy Lunar (I'm picturing a former Marukani messenger teamed up with a Solar chef and now I kinda want to play Exalted: The Pizza Delivery Game, by the way) wasn't possible. That's a pretty broad and diverse set of inspirations to draw from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T05:09:19-08:00","id":7981,"title":"","content":"I don't really mind getting shoehorn into being warrior and trickster; shaman,however, keep make me think about barbarian in loin-cloth talking about crazy shit that no one care about, or more specifically: Retard Baboon<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://i.minus.com/iblLyTxiNtvtT0.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum