:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://i.minus.com/iblLyTxiNtvtT0.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>So I take it you weren't there when Holden has put out his lengthy explenation how loin-cloth and crazy shit talking is necessary and compeltely integral to Lunars?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/620-arrakiz","name":"Arrakiz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar620_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T06:37:10-08:00","id":8024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arrakiz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=7998#post7998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I take it you weren't there when Holden has put out his lengthy explenation how loin-cloth and crazy shit talking is necessary and compeltely integral to Lunars?</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems like a self serving misrepresentation to a nuanced and complex explanation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T07:15:45-08:00","id":8037,"title":"","content":"Holden has defended Lunars having a barbarian aesthetic.<br /> With the definition of &quot;barbarian&quot; here being real world cultures that were commonly defined as such rather than the class in Dungeons and Dragons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T07:40:20-08:00","id":8059,"title":"","content":"Yeah. &quot;Barbarian&quot; for the purposes of Lunars not only includes Conan knock-offs but groups like the Turks, Aztecs, Iroquois, Mongols, Vikings, Huns, Celts, Irish, Navajos and depending on who you talked to back in the day, the Greeks (for the Persians) and the Egyptians (for the Romans). It is a group that's othered by the local, more powerful central state around. The Celts, Huns and Egyptians to the Romans, the Mongols, Japanese and Ryukyus to the Chinese.<br /> <br /> Now this can include your Conan knock-offs, but then if you go by actual novel source material that's not so much a bad thing.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T08:01:29-08:00","id":8082,"title":"","content":"I watch those 3rd Lunar preview thread really carefully so I know that the dev won' turn Lunars into ass-wiping retard baboon. The artists, however........ :Look at all the shirtless loin-cloth artwork in Manuel:Lunars: ....Urrgghhh","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T08:15:56-08:00","id":8101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorkaisChosen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=7988#post7988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Among many other things it makes me think of Odin in this context, so... no problems here. (I'd <i>also</i> see Odin as a Twilight; it depends on whether you want to emphasise &quot;mysterious wanderer&quot; or &quot;glorious and terrible god-king.&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div>As of <i>American Gods</i>, I see Odin as a <i>Fiend</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T08:46:22-08:00","id":8113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=8082#post8082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I watch those 3rd Lunar preview thread really carefully so I know that the dev won' turn Lunars into ass-wiping retard baboon. The artists, however........ :Look at all the shirtless loin-cloth artwork in Manuel:Lunars: ....Urrgghhh</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... yes. The edition that didn't do a great job of depicting the Lunars in a subtle and nuanced fashion <i>didn't do a great job of depicting the Lunars in a subtle and nuanced fashion.</i> The devteam's input doesn't stop the moment an artist picks up their sketching pencil.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=8101#post8101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As of <i>American Gods</i>, I see Odin as a <i>Fiend</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>The inspiration for that comes from the myths, AFAIK - there are some points where Odin is basically a dick. I tended to look at them as &quot;god-king being a dick&quot; hence Solar, but the Fiend version works too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T09:46:43-08:00","id":8158,"title":"","content":"I don't think there are supposed to be any Lunars in that picture, it's just a typical scene in Halta.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T21:05:18-08:00","id":9448,"title":"","content":"Man, all of this discussion about which characters should be what splats makes me think: wouldn't it be nice if there were multiple valid ways to emulate a character or capability, and the game <i>didn't</i> go out of its way at every turn to tell you that most of them are Doing It Wrong?<br /> <br /> On the original topic, I don't see Warrior/Trickster/Shaman as necessarily any more constraining than the Castes of other splats, which can all cover pretty broad thematic ground. The issue in 2e was that any theme outside of Werebeast Ragemonster was badly supported, and I'm hoping this fresh start can give all the other concepts the grounding they deserve. That said, having three castes instead of five does make it a bit harder for players to avoid stepping on each others' toes unless each Attribute cascade is considerably more diverse than before (or if there's now value in redundancy instead of just needing one massive dicepool per group per Ability). Aside, it also makes it a bit awkward to put a persistent group together when all the fluff holds that Lunars are RUGGED INDIVIDUALIST SURVIVORS and REALLY DAMN TERRITORIAL and furthermore that packs generally assemble for one mission then disband as soon as it's done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T03:44:04-08:00","id":9568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=8101#post8101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As of <i>American Gods</i>, I see Odin as a <i>Fiend</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>While Odin and Thor are quite capable of being utter dicks to everyone and everything, they're both fundamentally heroes. They are, point of fact, DESTINED heroes. Odin in the traditional sense is a Zenith. A polished politician and preacher, constantly appearing before men likely to become his Einherjar to compel them to feats of greatness or foolhardy.<br /> <br /> Thor is a classical Dawn, good at fighting and fucking and drinking and little else. Most of the Norse pantheon leans towards Zenith and Dawn in archetype, which is logical when you consider the pantheon exists to fight the most glorious battle ever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T04:50:26-08:00","id":9592,"title":"","content":"All Exalts are heroes. This is established.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T04:53:52-08:00","id":9593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=9592#post9592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All Exalts are heroes. This is established.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except Panther. He's just a dick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/698-chalicier","name":"chalicier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T06:14:13-08:00","id":9619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=9592#post9592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All Exalts are heroes. This is established.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of them are antiheroes. Abyssals and Inferanls come to mind. A fair amount of Lunars to. And even some Solars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/620-arrakiz","name":"Arrakiz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar620_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T06:24:46-08:00","id":9623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arrakiz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=9619#post9619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of them are antiheroes. Abyssals and Inferanls come to mind. A fair amount of Lunars to. And even some Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Antihero is just the negation of heroism. The common, unremarkable people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T06:43:13-08:00","id":9631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=9623#post9623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Antihero is just the negation of heroism. The common, unremarkable people.</div> </div> </div> </div>But I thought anti-hero is gritty dude who dress in leather and make the hard choice like &quot;I have to sacrifice my grandma to save the village!!!!!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T06:45:50-08:00","id":9633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=9631#post9631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I thought anti-hero is gritty dude who dress in leather and make the hard choice like &quot;I have to sacrifice my grandma to save the village!!!!!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the popular use, based on the word &quot;hero&quot; meaning a person full of moral virtues. Which is not the term exalted uses at all. Hero is the exceptional and driven. Antihero is whoever lacks that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T06:53:56-08:00","id":9640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=9633#post9633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the popular use, based on the word &quot;hero&quot; meaning a person full of moral virtues. Which is not the term exalted uses at all. Hero is the exceptional and driven. Antihero is whoever lacks that.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're right, then I was reffering to the second way it's usually used.<br /> <br /> Here's the question- can there be Exalts with no heroic drive? As in, people who do not have great ambitions, but through sheer way the events unfold find themselves in the middle of an epic story?<br /> <br /> And alternatively, can there be Exalts with heroic drive but unable to use it? People who find themselves in situation where they cannot do anything really epic, even though they'd love to? Do they counts as Exalts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/620-arrakiz","name":"Arrakiz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar620_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T06:58:22-08:00","id":9648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=9448#post9448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the original topic, I don't see Warrior/Trickster/Shaman as necessarily any more constraining than the Castes of other splats, which can all cover pretty broad thematic ground.</div> </div> </div> </div>Point of order? That is not the original topic. That is the tangent Arrakiz launched into in his opinionated-critique-presented-as-fact take on my approach to this thread. Which has subsequently eaten this thread. I would <i>love</i> for that to spin off into a thread of its own -- there's clear interest -- and for things to get back on the original topic, or for this thread to die if nobody's actually interested.<br /> <br /> The original topic was people's thoughts on what the Lunar physicality direction means and cool ideas that could it contain for Trickster and Shaman archetypes. With an emphasis on the latter. This was predominantly supposed to be a &quot;Cool stuff for Lunar Tricksters and Shamans given the physicality angle,&quot; thread. I apparently failed miserably in voicing that properly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T07:01:34-08:00","id":9650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arrakiz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=9640#post9640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're right, then I was reffering to the second way it's usually used.<br /> <br /> Here's the question- can there be Exalts with no heroic drive? As in, people who do not have great ambitions, but through sheer way the events unfold find themselves in the middle of an epic story?</div> </div> </div> </div>The capacity to pull off whatever is needed to survive and thrive in such epic story is indicative of the heroic potential of all exalts.<br /> Having &quot;no drive&quot; surely happens, I feel, but only in the context of being plenty satisfied. The retired hero, the happy ending before second season starts. If something pops that riles them from their comfort zone, they are as fierce and determined as any other exalt.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arrakiz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=9640#post9640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And alternatively, can there be Exalts with heroic drive but unable to use it? People who find themselves in situation where they cannot do anything really epic, even though they'd love to? Do they counts as Exalts?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're sticking too much to results and to appearances. &quot;epic&quot; is being thrown around too much.<br /> <br /> Exaltation is the realization of heroic potential at a crucial moment. It doesn't have to be immediate, but you'll definitely see it when you look back through such character's story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T07:19:24-08:00","id":9663,"title":"","content":"Well, we all got a bit baited into derailing the topic.<br /> <br /> For what it's worth, my two cents on physicality - I didn't really love what I read about the plans for Lunars from the devs at first. But that was mostly due to me mentally equalling &quot;physicality&quot; to &quot;brute force&quot;, which is stupid. This thread has helped me in that regard, because once I was actually forced to stop and think about it more than 3 seconds, I realized my initial assumption was, well... dumb.<br /> Physicality is, as I now understand, meant as opposed to the unreal, and the metaphysical flavor other Exalts might have, so this is where the &quot;no illusions&quot; doctrine came in, I think. I didn't like that at first as well.<br /> But I now see how it makes sense. Lunars are physical beings, so they don't craft illusions, that's what Raksha do. But that doesn't mean they can't trick people. A Lunar might shape himself into something else to fool an opponent, so he'll actually change shape, instead of crafting an illusion, which makes sense for, well, shapeshifters.<br /> <br /> <br /> So this physicality actually lends itself well to tricksters, who might be able to wear another's face to fool their victims, become supernaturally desirable or terrifying, use their magically honed body to perform feats of great dexterity, pickpocketing things that shouldn't be able to be stolen, though I'm still having difficulties to come up with tons of ideas in the broader sense.<br /> Shamans might fashion a tincture out of their blood that lets one perceive spirits after consumption? I'm not great at this, but I see how sticking to a physical, and &quot;real&quot; set of powers can still leave them with a huge variety of capabilities, and by now, I'm really excited and looking forward to it, and my initial disappointment has completely vanished.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T07:43:57-08:00","id":9680,"title":"","content":"You know how physicality lends well to shamans? They can turn into a bird. Or a towring 7 feet tall beast and rip someone apart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/620-arrakiz","name":"Arrakiz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar620_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T08:00:41-08:00","id":9692,"title":"","content":"Spirits become awfully physical if one can force them to materialize or punch them in the face regardless. Lunar No Moons can also offer physical solutions to problems, such as by healing injuries, creating shelters and wards, transforming their enemies into beasts, or blighting the Realm with sickness and poison.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T08:35:02-08:00","id":9723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arrakiz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=9680#post9680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know how physicality lends well to shamans? They can turn into a bird. Or a towring 7 feet tall beast and rip someone apart.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seeing as how many parts of the natural world are considered to have great sway over cultures, the former is actually quite relevant. The Romans considered the flight of birds to be of great import, and, well, the Realm borrows an awful lot from Rome, so that's quite far from an irrelevant observation. Speaking of Italy, <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Benandanti#Members\" target=\"_blank\">Benandanti.</a><br /> <br /> There's also the W:tA angle of &quot;spirit and flesh are unified&quot;, among others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T09:16:17-08:00","id":9752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arrakiz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=9640#post9640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's the question- can there be Exalts with no heroic drive? As in, people who do not have great ambitions, but through sheer way the events unfold find themselves in the middle of an epic story?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. One of the requirements for Exaltation is the will to use power in achieving their goals. People without ambition lack that drive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And alternatively, can there be Exalts with heroic drive but unable to use it? People who find themselves in situation where they cannot do anything really epic, even though they'd love to? Do they counts as Exalts? </div> </div> </div>The typical great act that triggers Exaltation is not a necessity. Only the greatness inherent in the person is absolutely required.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T09:39:10-08:00","id":9770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=9752#post9752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. One of the requirements for Exaltation is the will to use power in achieving their goals. People without ambition lack that drive.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. Well, flag that under &quot;things I wish were revised and changed in 3e&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/620-arrakiz","name":"Arrakiz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar620_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T09:44:52-08:00","id":9775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arrakiz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=9770#post9770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. Well, flag that under &quot;things I wish were revised and changed in 3e&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>You want Exalts to occasionally be couch potatoes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T10:36:08-08:00","id":9816,"title":"","content":"We have plenty of examples of that happening to various DBs in the books...why not? Do we really know for sure that particular fact *isn't* changing? I think it's about time we abandon the ideas holding over from 2E unless we have evidence that said factoids aren't changing. It's so much more useful to examine the game and what it could be *without* preconceptions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/748-ultrafennec","name":"UltraFennec","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar748_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T10:51:27-08:00","id":9831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>UltraFennec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=9816#post9816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We have plenty of examples of that happening to various DBs in the books...why not?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not aware of any DBs that aren't pursuing their own ambitions. Even the Slug is running a network of spies and informants and pushing a political agenda. The scope of those ambitions differ, sure, but that doesn't mean they don't have them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T10:54:58-08:00","id":9834,"title":"","content":"Really, even the Slug isn't a couch potato - he's driven in his goals to amass wealth and power. It's just that he eschews physical prowess in his pursuit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T17:05:06-08:00","id":10083,"title":"","content":"There's room for it; from Conan to the Black Company to a thousand other sources, shamans have definitely made threats to turn folks into unpleasant things before. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T17:19:18-08:00","id":10089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=9775#post9775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You want Exalts to occasionally be couch potatoes?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think he wants Exalts to occasionally be Han Solo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T17:26:06-08:00","id":10092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=10089#post10089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think he wants Exalts to occasionally be Han Solo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Han Solo is already badass when the movies start. He's a smuggler who makes a living doing dangerous things for money. He's set records on the Kessel run, owes a huge debt to a mobster, and shoots first and asks questions later.<br /> <br /> He isn't lacking for ambition in any way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T17:35:45-08:00","id":10097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=9834#post9834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's just that he eschews physical prowess in his pursuit.</div> </div> </div> </div>He doesn't eschew it, he's not capable of it because a spirit tore half of his leg out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T20:00:41-08:00","id":10157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=10089#post10089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think he wants Exalts to occasionally be Han Solo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, y'know, gods forbid, Achilles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T20:24:17-08:00","id":10162,"title":"","content":"I would like for Lunar's to also be able to enact physical changes in other people still, tricksters in mythology do that fairly often. One of their charm names can be monkey snatches peach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T20:58:24-08:00","id":10177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arrakiz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=9680#post9680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know how physicality lends well to shamans? They can turn into a bird. Or a towring 7 feet tall beast and rip someone apart.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but they can take on aspects of spirits by taking them into their bodies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T21:00:29-08:00","id":10178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=9448#post9448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, all of this discussion about which characters should be what splats makes me think: wouldn't it be nice if there were multiple valid ways to emulate a character or capability, and the game <i>didn't</i> go out of its way at every turn to tell you that most of them are Doing It Wrong?</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't be silly, the game does nothing of the sort.<br /> <br /> ...That's what OTHER PEOPLE do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T22:07:58-08:00","id":10208,"title":"","content":"~~<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=10157#post10157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, y'know, gods forbid, Achilles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Before the Trojan War, Achilles was already known as a great warrior and he threw a pretty epic fit for a spoiled rich kid. When he found a reason to fight in the conflict again? He went and massacred the Trojan army and their greatest hero. He was only inactive for a brief and significant stretch of time, much like an Exalt in Limit Break.<br /> ~~<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hanged Man</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> This is a bit of particularly obnoxious nerdrage, and I really do apologize, but it's coming out of me whether any of us want it to.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">A lot has been made about how Parsecs are distance, not time, and that indicates he went way closer to all these black holes, blah blah. In the original script, where Han is talking about the Kessel run? The stage direction for Luke is something like &quot;rolls his eyes at this huckster's obvious technobabble&quot;. The idea of that scene was that Han was <i>trying to con a couple desert yokels, but fumbled his social roll and managed to just sound full of shit instead</i>. When he actually turns out to be a legitimately heroic figure<i>,</i> it was supposed to be a total surprise to everyone, <i>including himself</i>. It was meant to make us look back at Obi Wan deciding to fly with this obviously crappy person, and wonder what the Force had shown him of Han's <i>unrealized</i> potential.<br /> All that crap about the Kessel run and the Maw is just as much of a retcon as Greedo firing first, or &quot;General&quot; Chewbacca being Yoda's best friend before his luck went sour. It's in the canon now, and I can't fight that, but it's not the same story that Lucas originally tried to tell, and in my opinion it's weaker because of it.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> I just go with what I saw on the screen. Maybe Luke couldn't pull off the eye-roll and maybe Han is too charming for me to not buy into the reputation (and I know what a parasec is!). Besides, even if we are supposed to believe that Han Solo is a crappy space smuggler, he's still an active, ambitious space smuggler. He's not drowning his sorrows in a cantina somewhere waiting for a bounty hunter to kill him, he's looking to find a way to pay his debts off.<br /> <br /> The idea that any Exalt would rather sit and watch the world turn is antithetical to the setting. The Exalted are doers. They act.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T00:11:22-08:00","id":10250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=10157#post10157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, y'know, gods forbid, Achilles.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean the demigod who when presented with a choice between a long happy life of obscurity and short but glorious life, chose the latter? That Achilles?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/370-oriares","name":"Oriares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T01:14:54-08:00","id":10256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=10092#post10092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Han Solo is already badass when the movies start. He's a smuggler who makes a living doing dangerous things for money. He's set records on the Kessel run, owes a huge debt to a mobster, and shoots first and asks questions later.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not the point.<br /> <br /> The point is that he's not in this for your revolution.<br /> <br /> Yet he still wound up there, and ended up doing great things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">He isn't lacking for ambition in any way.</div> </div> </div> </div>What exactly was Han's ambition beyond &quot;get enough money to pay off his debt&quot;, which is about as ambitious as trying to pay off your mortgage?<br /> <br /> I guess Luke compels him for a while with the idea that he might become rich, but his personality at that point suggests that that means early retirement.<br /> <br /> Depending on exactly how large Han's debt is supposed to be; Luke does seem to suggest that the price he asks for (and is hoping to go square with Jabba with) would be sufficient to purchase their own ship, but I couldn't say whether an interstellar ships is equivalent to a used car or a private plane in that economy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T01:20:45-08:00","id":10258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=10208#post10208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea that any Exalt would rather sit and watch the world turn is antithetical to the setting. The Exalted are doers. They act.</div> </div> </div> </div>Objection! A Cincinnatus or Washington type that moves and shakes the world when - and exactly to the degree - necessary and then goes home to raise olives and grow sheep should <i>totally</i> be a valid concept for an Exalt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T01:36:33-08:00","id":10263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=10208#post10208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">~~<br /> The idea that any Exalt would rather sit and watch the world turn is antithetical to the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Demetheus has often been portrayed as turning into an indolent drunk in response to Kidal's death.<br /> <br /> To proscribe that Exalted only ever act in this particular, specific way is to rob them of empathy and literary resonance, and to make the setting <i>less</i> credible because the setting just does not look like how it would if the Exalted were as universally driven as some people seem to think they should be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T02:01:24-08:00","id":10273,"title":"","content":"The Exalted are people of such grand influence, their inaction itself may shape the world.<br /> <br /> Any time in fiction where you see someone whose actions could change the course of events refuse to act, that is appropriate to Exalted. <br /> <br /> And what of Gotham City when Batman hangs his cape? Whatever Happens to the Man of Tomorrow and the world he leaves behind?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T06:38:12-08:00","id":10359,"title":"","content":"~~<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=10258#post10258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Objection! A Cincinnatus or Washington type that moves and shakes the world when - and exactly to the degree - necessary and then goes home to raise olives and grow sheep should <i>totally</i> be a valid concept for an Exalt.</div> </div> </div> </div> Note the two actions you listed. Washington, from what I understand, had a pretty good operation going - IIRC, his booze was in high demand. He didn't spend the rest of his life sitting on his but eating grapes and being fanned by slave girls. He just moved his activity to a different theater.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=10263#post10263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Demetheus has often been portrayed as turning into an indolent drunk in response to Kidal's death.</div> </div> </div> </div>For how long? Does he spend the rest of his life doing nothing but boozing? I seem to recall that he eventually gets pulled out of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To proscribe that Exalted only ever act in this particular, specific way is to rob them of empathy and literary resonance, and to make the setting <i>less</i> credible because the setting just does not look like how it would if the Exalted were as universally driven as some people seem to think they should be. </div> </div> </div> I'm not saying all the Exalted are equally driven. I'm saying they all have drive. They all will use their powers to advance themselves in some way. People who would be literal layabouts aren't worthy of Exaltation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=10273#post10273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Exalted are people of such grand influence, their inaction itself may shape the world.<br /> <br /> Any time in fiction where you see someone whose actions could change the course of events refuse to act, that is appropriate to Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but notice that you are already marking them as people of action. Sure, moments or even years of inaction can be appropriate for characters, but an Exalt will never be the kind of reject that spends his years quietly working at a dead-end job and then dies unremarked. Stick an Exalt in that dead-end job and he will either force his way up the ladder or he'll go find a better job.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And what of Gotham City when Batman hangs his cape? Whatever Happens to the Man of Tomorrow and the world he leaves behind? </div> </div> </div>Comic book Batman will retire the day after he dies. The Dark Knight Rises Batman isn't going to stay retired.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T07:13:14-08:00","id":10385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=10263#post10263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Demetheus has often been portrayed as turning into an indolent drunk in response to Kidal's death.<br /> <br /> To proscribe that Exalted only ever act in this particular, specific way is to rob them of empathy and literary resonance, and to make the setting <i>less</i> credible because the setting just does not look like how it would if the Exalted were as universally driven as some people seem to think they should be.</div> </div> </div> </div>His constant emo-face attract the attention of a neomah, a horny hell-nun and Burning Feather so the guy must have some epic whining hiding inside of him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T07:37:48-08:00","id":10396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=10359#post10359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">~~<br /> For how long? Does he spend the rest of his life doing nothing but boozing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Who cares? What exactly is &quot;the rest of his life&quot;? The man is capable of living several lifetimes worth of indolence or depression.<br /> <br /> The idea of Exalted who spend their entire lives doing nothing of note is no more credible than the idea that anybody would live like that.<br /> <br /> And where they would, one should examine their reasons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying all the Exalted are equally driven. I'm saying they all have drive. They all will use their powers to advance themselves in some way.</div> </div> </div> </div>And when they achieve their goals?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">People who would be literal layabouts aren't worthy of Exaltation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not all Exalted patrons are the Maidens.<br /> <br /> This, mind, is a tangent that severely misunderstands Arrakiz' question.<br /> <br /> Take a look:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arrakiz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As in, people who do not have great ambitions, but through sheer way the events unfold find themselves in the middle of an epic story?</div> </div> </div> </div>Han Solo wound up in the story of fighting the empire by accident. He didn't go looking for it, but it found him, and he made good on it.<br /> <br /> That's the question Arrakiz asked, and it's a perfectly valid thing for Exalted to be, either in their becoming or in the course of their lives.<br /> <br /> I'd also cite Jubai, who didn't go looking for the Eight Devils of Kimon, but happened upon one of them assaulting a retainer for a local official, then got roped in by a government agent who recognised his skills, and became a bit more invested when he realised he had a personal stake based on an unfinished grudge.<br /> <br /> In my vision of the First Age, that's actually one of the roles of the Sidereal Exalted; they find the Jubais among the Lawgivers and arrange for them to get involved in things. It seems appropriate for their set up.<br /> <br /> And even in this fallen Age, there are people and beings who'll always notice the Exalted, and account for them, and push and pull them towards and away from their own ends.<br /> <br /> They'll do the same for mortals, and one another, mind; the world has trouble being big enough for anybody to get by as an island.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T09:55:32-08:00","id":10512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=10396#post10396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Who cares? What exactly is &quot;the rest of his life&quot;? The man is capable of living several lifetimes worth of indolence or depression.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point is that his drunken state is a temporary thing. It is not a defining part of who he is. He's got a lot of grief and guilt to drown, but he'll get over it eventually.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The idea of Exalted who spend their entire lives doing nothing of note is no more credible than the idea that anybody would live like that.<br /> <br /> And where they would, one should examine their reasons. </div> </div> </div>I know plenty of people who are content with their lives. They don't want to change their situation even though it could be better. They don't aspire to do anything particularly special. These people do not qualify to be Exalts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And when they achieve their goals? </div> </div> </div>They find a new goal, even if that goal is &quot;defend what I have accomplished&quot;. The current champion boxer doesn't get to stay the top dog without hard work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Han Solo wound up in the story of fighting the empire by accident. He didn't go looking for it, but it found him, and he made good on it.<br /> <br /> That's the question Arrakiz asked, and it's a perfectly valid thing for Exalted to be, either in their becoming or in the course of their lives.<br /> <br /> I'd also cite Jubai, who didn't go looking for the Eight Devils of Kimon, but happened upon one of them assaulting a retainer for a local official, then got roped in by a government agent who recognised his skills, and became a bit more invested when he realised he had a personal stake based on an unfinished grudge. </div> </div> </div>I guess I misunderstood the question. Yes, I can see an Exalt whose goals are not all that grand ending up being swept up in a bigger story. My point still stands, though. Exalts are people who are willing to use their powers to further their goals. They are people who do things, not people who wait for others to do things for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T11:32:30-08:00","id":10600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=10359#post10359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">~~Note the two actions you listed. Washington, from what I understand, had a pretty good operation going - IIRC, his booze was in high demand. He didn't spend the rest of his life sitting on his but eating grapes and being fanned by slave girls. He just moved his activity to a different theater.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but not really germane to the example of their behavior in the public sphere. Or to the argument I perceive you as making, which would outlaw any such concept as, say, a father who wanted to make sure his daughters were happy, or the badass Sword Saint who knows not what it means to cut a man twice and spends his days in contemplation of the cherry blossoms.<br /> <br /> Or, for that matter, as my own Dawn, whose highest ambition is to retire and run an inn, as long as her people can be safe while she does it.<br /> <br /> Not only is that kind of personally irritating, I think it's very questionable storytelling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T11:44:45-08:00","id":10619,"title":"","content":"You are confusing choosing to act instead of running away, with having a clear goal you're trying to acomplish. First is just courage, the second is ambition. Just because you act when you're pushed against the wall, doesn't mean you have an actual ambition.<br /> <br /> I'd say that Exalts are generally categorised as people who get drawn into epic events, not as people who pursue activity in epic events, because, well... You won't hear about those Exalts who don't act. You'll only hear about those who are cought in the tides of the history, regardless of whether they have a goal to acomplish or not.<br /> <br /> And, case in point, I know my players. Having them come up with and roleplay characters with real ambitions is something of a problem. They just can't do it well. They either overplay and go super over-the-top cliche, or get lost and quickly abbandon what was supposed to be a driving force. So that's just something I have to deal with, I'd rather the game helped me deal with it, or at least not tried to make it harder by saying &quot;your character abso-freakin-lutely has to be ambitious&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/620-arrakiz","user":"Arrakiz","date":". 11-14-2013, 02:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/620-arrakiz","name":"Arrakiz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar620_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T12:56:08-08:00","id":10701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=10600#post10600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, but not really germane to the example of their behavior in the public sphere. Or to the argument I perceive you as making, which would outlaw any such concept as, say, a father who wanted to make sure his daughters were happy, or the badass Sword Saint who knows not what it means to cut a man twice and spends his days in contemplation of the cherry blossoms.<br /> <br /> Or, for that matter, as my own Dawn, whose highest ambition is to retire and run an inn, as long as her people can be safe while she does it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It sounds to me like your examples here are easily compatible with my views. The father has a purpose for which he acts and acts well. Sure, he probably wouldn't normally Exalt, but I can see events forcing him up to a level where he earns it without changing his goals in life. The sword saint must have done a lot of training and activity to get where he is and philosophical or artistic meditation is certainly a worthwhile thing. Your Dawn clearly wants to do something with her life.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arrakiz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=10619#post10619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are confusing choosing to act instead of running away, with having a clear goal you're trying to acomplish. First is just courage, the second is ambition. Just because you act when you're pushed against the wall, doesn't mean you have an actual ambition.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you had to be pushed against the wall in order to act and only take the fastest route out of the crisis you can see, you don't have what it takes to be Exalted.<br /> <br /> When the Millenium Falcon is trapped on the Death Star and Luke finds out that Princess Leia is on board, Han helps with the rescue effort. He's doing it for the money, sure, but he's also staring down an entire space station full of stormtroopers. He's capable of doing hard things instead of just taking the easy way out. There is no gun to his head saying &quot;you must save the princess or else&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd say that Exalts are generally categorised as people who get drawn into epic events, not as people who pursue activity in epic events, because, well... You won't hear about those Exalts who don't act. You'll only hear about those who are cought in the tides of the history, regardless of whether they have a goal to acomplish or not.<br /> <br /> And, case in point, I know my players. Having them come up with and roleplay characters with real ambitions is something of a problem. They just can't do it well. They either overplay and go super over-the-top cliche, or get lost and quickly abbandon what was supposed to be a driving force. So that's just something I have to deal with, I'd rather the game helped me deal with it, or at least not tried to make it harder by saying &quot;your character abso-freakin-lutely has to be ambitious&quot;. </div> </div> </div>I think you are reading a greater level of activity into my statement that &quot;Exalts do things&quot; than I had implied. Not every Exalt wants to shake the pillars of Heaven or conquer the world, but they all have something they want out of life and they are active in getting it. If they are a Dragon-Blooded farmer and all they want to do with their life is manage the family farm, they are going to manage the family farm. If something happens to disrupt the family farm, though, they do something about it instead of hoping someone else will fix the problem. They go punch the local weather god to get a drought canceled, they stop an invading army, they assinate their greatest rival, whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T13:34:41-08:00","id":10729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=10701#post10701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It sounds to me like your examples here are easily compatible with my views. The father has a purpose for which he acts and acts well. Sure, he probably wouldn't normally Exalt, but I can see events forcing him up to a level where he earns it without changing his goals in life. The sword saint must have done a lot of training and activity to get where he is and philosophical or artistic meditation is certainly a worthwhile thing. Your Dawn clearly wants to do something with her life.</div> </div> </div> </div>They might be compatible with what you thought you had written. They are not compatible with what I believe I was reading prior to this post.<br /> <br /> As far as I can tell, no one is contesting that, if you show an Exalt a problem or opportunity, they will tend to solve it rather than ignoring it. Objections are being raised to the way your phrasing echoes the 'Epic Motivations' requirement in 2E, which is a problematic mechanic with which many people, myself included, disagree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T13:49:03-08:00","id":10740,"title":"","content":"Epic Motivations can die in a fire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T13:53:40-08:00","id":10744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=10740#post10740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Epic Motivations can die in a fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>You will note that this only confirms Valles's observation that your choice of phrasing rings self-contradictory. I'd advise explaining what your position is apart from this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T14:31:11-08:00","id":10783,"title":"","content":"I've based my position on the 2e core books list of &quot;what does it take to Exalt?&quot; The one pertinent here is the whole &quot;An Exalt is someone willing to use power&quot;. This is why no &quot;Anathema&quot; has ever been Exalted and then just sat on their hands for the rest of their life. They are the sort to put their power to use. They are active, rather than passive. They have ambition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T15:06:20-08:00","id":10809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=10740#post10740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Epic Motivations can die in a fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great! I'm glad that -<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've based my position on the 2e core books list of &quot;what does it take to Exalt?&quot; The one pertinent here is the whole &quot;An Exalt is someone willing to use power&quot;. This is why no &quot;Anathema&quot; has ever been Exalted and then just sat on their hands for the rest of their life. They are the sort to put their power to use. They are active, rather than passive. They have ambition. </div> </div> </div>...I'm not sure if you're trolling or you genuinely can't see that you're using <i>exactly</i> the same logic and language that gave us Epic Motivations in the first place. Either way, I don't see any point in my continuing the conversation. Have fun, folks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T15:27:37-08:00","id":10821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=10783#post10783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've based my position on the 2e core books list of &quot;what does it take to Exalt?&quot; The one pertinent here is the whole &quot;An Exalt is someone willing to use power&quot;. This is why no &quot;Anathema&quot; has ever been Exalted and then just sat on their hands for the rest of their life. They are the sort to put their power to use. They are active, rather than passive. They have ambition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, remember that really great song that's just one loud note sustained for five minutes?<br /> <br /> Or that fantastic book that's entirely composed of climaxes?<br /> <br /> Or that excellent movie that's just a <a href=\"http://qntm.org/screenplays\" target=\"_blank\">one hour fight scene</a>?<br /> <br /> I do not remember those things either, because they do not exist as things that were real and also good.<br /> <br /> The volume knob has lower settings. They are not there for decoration!<br /> <br /> If this is an unfair representation of your position \u2014 and I do sincerely believe and hope that it <i>is</i> \u2014 then I would advise you to actually explain your position in a manner that does not contradict itself between universal and particular statements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T15:39:40-08:00","id":10825,"title":"","content":"If a farmer Exalting and just staying a farmer all his life and just generally doing farming stuff, in your mind, counts as someone who has a goal and takes the necessary actions to achieve it, then I am genuinely curious to know what would be necessary in your mind for a character to be unambitious and passive. I don't think anyone in the history of everything as ever argued that an Exalted would just curl up in a ball and cry instead of punching the local weather god in the face until rain comes out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T15:40:08-08:00","id":10826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=10809#post10809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...I'm not sure if you're trolling or you genuinely can't see that you're using <i>exactly</i> the same logic and language that gave us Epic Motivations in the first place. Either way, I don't see any point in my continuing the conversation. Have fun, folks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Enh...I think there's a distinction there. It was not immediately obvious, but I think it's been teased out with time, and if I'm reading Kyeudo right, it's best demonstrated by am example:<br /> <br /> Say there were two farmers, Farmer A and Farmer B. Both are happy to sit on their farm, have a small family, grow vegetables. Neither have an Epic Motivation (unless it's, like, &quot;CABBAGES!!!&quot; or something). A Dragon-Blood and some bandits come by and burn the farms to the ground, and kill the farmers' families. The farmers stand up for themselves in a moment of heroism, but it's not enough.<br /> <br /> Now, in a purely hypothetical time-pause, Lytek or someone comes by and tells the farmers, &quot;I've got a shiny new Exaltation you can have. But first, I need to know what you'll do with it?&quot;<br /> <br /> Farmer A says, &quot;I'll get the biggest sword I can find and kill that Dragon-Blood and those bandits!,&quot; or &quot;I'll rebuild my farm, even better (or maybe just faster)!,&quot; or maybe &quot;I'll persuade kings and princes that this should never have come to pass and unite all the local provinces!,&quot; or perhaps &quot;I'll fill out the VERY BEST forms I can to petition the government for financial aid packages!,&quot; or &quot;Fuck farming, I'ma learn Sorcery!&quot;, or any of a million other things.<br /> <br /> Farmer B says, &quot;Eh, I'll probably go lie down, have some drinks, maybe cry a little. Eventually, I might get up and putter around, or fix things up a bit, though I'm in no hurry, and I might starve to death first. You know, maybe instead of Exalting me, you could make all of this just not have happened...?&quot;<br /> <br /> Farmer A Exalts, and still doesn't necessarily have an Epic Motivation. Farmer B does not.<br /> <br /> I'll admit that it might be a silly distinction-- I can imagine a lot of people having trouble imagining that Farmer B would even exist. But I -think- it was the distinction being made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/926-yishten","name":"Yishten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar926_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T15:49:54-08:00","id":10834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yishten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=10826#post10826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Farmer A Exalts, and still doesn't necessarily have an Epic Motivation. Farmer B does not.<br /> <br /> I'll admit that it might be a silly distinction-- I can imagine a lot of people having trouble imagining that Farmer B would even exist. But I -think- it was the distinction being made.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T15:54:23-08:00","id":10843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=10821#post10821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If this is an unfair representation of your position \u2014 and I do sincerely believe and hope that it <i>is</i> \u2014 then I would advise you to actually explain your position in a manner that does not contradict itself between universal and particular statements.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um, yes, I would say that you've missed my point completely. I'm not saying that every Dragon-Blood wants to do something world-shattering or is always involved in politics or something like that. I'm trying to get across that all of them approach their problems in life as things that they can do something about rather than as things they hope will go away. If traffic on the freeway is bad and that's the biggest problem they have in life, they will be trying to do something about it. Add an extra lane, find a different route to work, murder a million people to reduce the number of drivers - whatever takes their particular fancy.<br /> <br /> Someone once said &quot;Reasonable people adapt themselves to their situation, while unreasonable people try to adapt the situation to themselves. Progress, therefore, relies upon unreasonable people.&quot; Exalts are all unreasonable people.<br /> <br /> A common proverb is &quot;May God grant me the courage to change the things that I can change, the patience to accept the things I cannot change, and the wisdom to know the difference.&quot; Exalts skip the wisdom part because there is nothing they can't change if they try hard enough and they know it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=10809#post10809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...I'm not sure if you're trolling or you genuinely can't see that you're using <i>exactly</i> the same logic and language that gave us Epic Motivations in the first place. Either way, I don't see any point in my continuing the conversation. Have fun, folks.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I was trolling, I'd be doing a much poorer job of annoying people. I suck at trolling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=10825#post10825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a farmer Exalting and just staying a farmer all his life and just generally doing farming stuff, in your mind, counts as someone who has a goal and takes the necessary actions to achieve it, then I am genuinely curious to know what would be necessary in your mind for a character to be unambitious and passive. I don't think anyone in the history of everything as ever argued that an Exalted would just curl up in a ball and cry instead of punching the local weather god in the face until rain comes out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yishten did a good job of explaining it.<br /> <br /> There are people (probably including myself) that just sort of hope their problems will go away. They rely on other people to do the hard things. If they lose their jobs, they go through the motions of finding a new one while they sit on a couch and drink beer, simply waiting for someone to contact them. Other people lose their jobs and decide to start their own buisness or go out and meet prospective employers personally. These are the people who see something requiring real work and do it anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":74,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","user":"Kyeudo","date":". 11-14-2013, 07:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T15:55:25-08:00","id":10846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yishten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=10826#post10826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll admit that it might be a silly distinction-- I can imagine a lot of people having trouble imagining that Farmer B would even exist. But I -think- it was the distinction being made.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that that is probably the position being aimed for. Unfortunately, I had to arrive at that conclusion by deduction, since that's not what he's <i>saying</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T16:03:16-08:00","id":10860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=10846#post10846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree that that is probably the position being aimed for. Unfortunately, I had to arrive at that conclusion by deduction, since that's not what he's <i>saying</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's a delicate point I'm trying to make and I have a non-standard thought process and lots of clumsy words to work with. I'm not surprised when I start spouting gibberish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T18:13:13-08:00","id":10954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=10860#post10860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It's a delicate point I'm trying to make and I have a non-standard thought process and lots of clumsy words to work with. I'm not surprised when I start spouting gibberish.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's something be said for the hero who is content to remain at peace until war encroaches upon his doorstep as much as there is for the wandering swordsman seeking a cause.<br /> <br /> They may seem diametrically opposed, but the former is the traditional farmer-general of Western archetype. The latter is the itinerant hero of Eastern tradition. Is either one necessarily more correct than the other? I don't believe so.<br /> <br /> Most people wouldn't argue that Odin and Thor aren't heroes. But they spend most of their time sitting around drinking, pulling pranks on mortals, and, well, farming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T20:29:20-08:00","id":11026,"title":"","content":"The problem is the autonomous process of Exalted and the shards brought in with 2E. In 1E if you Exalted it was that you were chosen or were born into it with the case of Dragonblooded. This needs to return. Also the reason you're chosen is because you've the potential for greater, and you will come to it whether you know it or not. There is such a thing called Fate after all. With the case of Han Solo. He'd Exalt because in his future he is a big damn hero, and plays a large role in taking down the Empire. Your country bumbkin can Exalt, your farmer can Exalt, but by Exalting you will cause a shift in the status quo. You are a power player, whether you know it or not yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T00:22:44-08:00","id":11099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=7217#post7217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed. Lunars are not the Brood Queen or Alex Mercer.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm curious if there is any exalt type who would represent that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/726-amine-hsu","name":"Amine Hsu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar726_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T01:03:35-08:00","id":11109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amine Hsu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=11099#post11099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm curious if there is any exalt type who would represent that.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Infernals? They're the other splat that had shapeshifting in 2e anyway.<br /> <br /> Although... eating people to take their form is (as far as I can tell) one of Alex Mercer's main schticks... is the Sacred Hunt going away? (please please please?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T02:57:22-08:00","id":11136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amine Hsu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=11099#post11099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm curious if there is any exalt type who would represent that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cthulhu body horror is the Infernal stick now which make me an even happier Venus. I gonna create a Kimberian Defiler that shit exploding fetus like machine gun at those onceborn woman inside the Neverborn tomb.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T05:50:11-08:00","id":11207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=11109#post11109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...Infernals? They're the other splat that had shapeshifting in 2e anyway.<br /> <br /> Although... eating people to take their form is (as far as I can tell) one of Alex Mercer's main schticks... is the Sacred Hunt going away? (please please please?)</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1e, the Abyssal disguise Charms weren't illusions. They also ate people and took their forms, but didn't have a library for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T06:45:11-08:00","id":11231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amine Hsu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=11099#post11099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious if there is any exalt type who would represent that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Liminal Exalted already patch themselves up with the flesh of the dead (including those they killed) in order to expand and improve the selves. They explicitly will have Flesh-aspected Charms that make this cadaver-incorporation process easier, so I can easily see them joining Lunars and Abyssals in the ranks of &quot;eat you to wear your face&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 11-17-2013, 09:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T08:34:23-08:00","id":11306,"title":"","content":"I wonder at Lunars who might conduct themselves in an interaction in the manner of Coyote in Gunnerkrigg Court, all shifting and twisting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T08:41:23-08:00","id":11310,"title":"","content":"What Attribute-based Charms are inspired by Coyote? Granted, his level of power is that of an elder, or a powerful god or demon, or a raksha in some degree of the Wyld, but if he were to make Exigents with Attribute-based Charms, what would those Charms look like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T08:46:47-08:00","id":11312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=11310#post11310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What Attribute-based Charms are inspired by Coyote? Granted, his level of power is that of an elder, or a powerful god or demon, or a raksha in some degree of the Wyld, but if he were to make Exigents with Attribute-based Charms, what would those Charms look like?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why Exigents? Isator explicitely mentioned him as the possibility of a Lunar inspiration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T08:53:05-08:00","id":11315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=11310#post11310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What Attribute-based Charms are inspired by Coyote?</div> </div> </div> </div>When I try to think about <i>why</i> Coyote would opt to twist and coil himself about while having a conversation, I imagine he's doing it to try and create a context in which the other person is made somewhat uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> I feel like it's the kind of thing that might be done in one or more Appearance Charms, maybe?<br /> <br /> I was just looking at the thread title and thinking &quot;what might be an example of a trickster character who is defined by a form of physicality&quot;, and my mind went to Coyote.<br /> <br /> Coyote who is a trickster, Coyote who can't keep still even when he's standing or sitting in place, Coyote whose majority of scenes are based around conversations he's having.<br /> <br /> Heck, he even has a glorious god-body, even if Annie needs to be in the ether to perceive it.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It feels like a good place to start, so the next step might be &quot;what kind of Charms would one imagine building a Lunar like Coyote out of&quot;?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Granted, his level of power is that of an elder</div> </div> </div> </div>I could certainly see tricks like rending great chasms in the earth with his claws or plucking the moon from the sky as high-Essence stunts (in the non-system sense of the word).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T09:53:21-08:00","id":11374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=11312#post11312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Why Exigents? Isator explicitely mentioned him as the possibility of a Lunar inspiration.</div> </div> </div> </div> Because I imagine that any Attribute-based Charms of Exigents produced by Coyote and Brier Rabbit would look a lot like Lunar Charms. And because neither Coyote or Brier Rabbit are Luna, exactly. Basically, I was trying to avoid one potential source of confusion and just stumbled into another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T16:07:56-08:00","id":11648,"title":"","content":"While this thread is waiting for further thoughts on tricksters and shamans, a brief thought on that whole tangent revisiting the topic of Exalted viability (for want of a better term):<br /> <br /> Anybody remember Fitter Happier's idea about a Dawn Caste who was just a regular farmer until the day Exaltation was bestowed on him and he became a warrior?<br /> <br /> 'Cause... that's basically David.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure why neither I nor anybody else recognised that at the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T16:33:20-08:00","id":11665,"title":"","content":"Can you call anyone a regular farmer when he makes a habit of chasing after lions and bears with a staff and sling to rescue his sheep?<br /> <br /> Seriously, he was a young man. If his father or supervisor was particularly unforgiving, he might have been abused for the loss, but would anyone with reasonable expectations have blamed him for just LETTING the large, powerful, ferocious beasts make off with a few of the stupid, smelly, bleating irritations? But no, David put in the long, long, long hours of practice to become a deadly crack-shot with his sling (making headshots from a distance while running!), and he developed the fleetness of foot and strength of limb that would let him run up to a stunned Goliath, take the giant's own sword, and cut off his head.<br /> <br /> Young pre-King David was already a warrior, even before he faced another man on the field of battle, even before other men recognized him as a warrior.<br /> <br /> <br /> Which is also part of Exaltation. The Dawn Exaltation sees that in shepherds like David. &quot;This is a kid that wants to fight for something, even unto death. He's already practicing for it, in his own ways!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, Levi, please insert a line-break above your signature, to seperate it from your post-text. It's really starting to bug me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 11-15-2013, 07:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T16:59:18-08:00","id":11689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=11665#post11665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Levi, please insert a line-break above your signature, to seperate it from your post-text. It's really starting to bug me.</div> </div> </div> </div>All the cool people are doing it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T17:57:29-08:00","id":11740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/7109-ex3-lunar-physicality-tricksters-shamans?p=11665#post11665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you call anyone a regular farmer when he makes a habit of chasing after lions and bears with a staff and sling to rescue his sheep?</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of? Those sheep are your livelihood; you don't find a way to protect them from wild beasts, you're going to starve.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">he developed the fleetness of foot and strength of limb that would let him run up to a stunned Goliath, take the giant's own sword, and cut off his head.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note, in this model, David is already Exalted by the time he faces Goliath.<br /> <br /> Also before he's called to the court of Saul to ward off depression and the torments of a wicked spirit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Young pre-King David was already a warrior, even before he faced another man on the field of battle, even before other men recognized him as a warrior.</div> </div> </div> </div>In most places outside of the Blessed Isle, being a farmer probably means you're living on the frontiers of the wilderness where it's you and the homestead against the weather and the animals and monsters and the more primal gods.<br /> <br /> Even if most of your day to day life is spent tilling the soil or making sure the livestock don't wander off.<br /> <br /> I don't really know where Fitter Happier placed his farmer, or how much he knows about the travails of farming before, say, the 14th century in Europe or whatever (and even then, you still had frontiers in places like Ireland where farming meant regular battles against the angry natives).<br /> <br /> The point is, the origin story of David is that one day, a prophet on a mission from God entered the house of his father, was shown all his elder brothers and told &quot;the last son is out tending the sheep&quot;, and when he entered the prophet was instructed to anoint him and the Holy Spirit was with him thereafter.<br /> <br /> Assume a God who opts not to use prophets going through the routine of deferring to the father and inspecting the other sons, and that story could easily be &quot;one day while David was tending his father's sheep, God decided he should be the next king of Israel and bestowed him with the Holy Spirit&quot;.<br /> <br /> That and how, if Fitter's desire for whether or not one is worthy of their Second Breath to be an open question, then the idea that nobody might know why he was so anointed until he slays a Philistine giant and collects the foreskins of 200 enemy warriors might contribute to that (and then laying with his subordinate's wife and sending him off to die might send it into doubt again).<br /> <br /> And the Age of Sorrows has been a time where the question never gets to be answered, because two weeks after you were Chosen the Wyld Hunt chased you down and skewered you like a boar*.<br /> <br /> Besides, I think to get too into arguments about what qualities David might have possessed by which he should have been recognised as a warrior kind of undermines &quot;Do not consider his appearance or his height, for I have rejected him. The Lord does not look at the things man looks at. Man look at the outward appearance, but the Lord looks at the heart.&quot;<br /> <br /> (I also kind of feel that talking about killing lions and bears as a comparison to killing a defiant enemy warrior is more a piece of homesy wisdom than a statement of &quot;I'm a badass&quot;, but that's just my opinion, and probably doesn't matter much)<br /> <br /> * Note to self: retain plot hook of young Solar whose ghost lingers in frustration about why they were Chosen since their really premature death never gave them a chance to really demonstrate worth in it, and entreats living Exalts to seek the Sun out and inquire after his reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}